{# A ROW OF HEADLINE FIGURES — four to a row, wherever the section draws one.

   A FIGURE THAT CANNOT BE MEASURED SAYS SO, and it says so where the number
   would have been: an em dash, with the caption carrying the reason. Zero is
   a measurement and this is the absence of one, and a row that drew them the
   same would report a quiet installation and an unconfigured one identically.

   THE CAPTION IS TWO FRAGMENTS. The second one is ink — the part that wants
   an eye — which is why the source hands them over separately and the colour
   is decided here. #}
<div class="grid kstrip">
    {%- for figure in figures -%}
        <div class="c kpi{{ figure.hot ? ' hot' }}">
            <span class="tab">{{ figure.label }}</span>
            <b class="disp">{{ figure.isMeasured ? figure.value : '—' }}
                {%- if figure.unit %}<em>{{ figure.unit }}</em>{% endif -%}
            </b>
            {%- if figure.caption or figure.warning -%}
                <span class="sub">
                    {{- figure.caption -}}
                    {%- if figure.caption and figure.warning %} &middot; {% endif -%}
                    {%- if figure.warning %}<span class="w">{{ figure.warning }}</span>{% endif -%}
                </span>
            {%- endif -%}
        </div>
    {%- endfor -%}
</div>
